ario (drawn at same x as Mario's column). The bubbles in the screenshot are around x=48, y=150-190 — yes matches (small circles). get_pixel_color(49,178) hit water because the circle is centered maybe at x=52? Fine.\n\nAnyway for the scene mapping, I have enough. But I want to confirm the two dark shapes. Let me query (212,204), (230,204), and also check sprite list at those pixels. Actually list_sprites showed no fish, so the shapes are background. Let me get tile at (212,204).\n\nLet me also capture a second screenshot to store as proof? The screenshot is already the proof. The prompt says \"The proof is a screenshot taken in the scene.\" I've taken it. Good.\n\nNow record the water scene mapping. Then move to castle 1-4.\n\nReach instructions for water: \"reset_emulator; while paused on the genuine title screen (game_mode $0770=0, logo visible), write_memory CPU $075F (1887)=1, $075C (1884)=1, $0760 (1888)=2; then play_input [{start,6},{none,300}]. The level-init area selector (CPU $9C13) reads world $075F=1 → world base table $9CB4[1]=5, adds $0760=2 → header index 7 = $9CBC[7]=$01 → area type $074E=0 (water palette selector 1 $8CA4), area index $074F=1 → 2-2 loads; $075C=1 makes the HUD read WORLD 2-2. Verified live: $075F=1,$075C=1,$0760=2,$074E=0,$074F=1. Screenshot paused at level opening.\" Important: must be genuine title, not attract demo (attract overwrites the selector bytes).\n\nWait, but actually a more careful reach: after reset, pause immediately, step 40 frames to reach the title logo. If the game is in attract, press Start once to return to title. Then write.\n\nHmm, in my run: I did reset+pause, got blank screen, stepped 40 → title logo. So the reach is: reset_emulator, pause_emulator (catch it before attract), step_frame 40 to settle the title, then write, then Start. But there's a risk the game enters attract if real time passes. As long as paused, it won't. Good. Actually reset+pause leaves it paused; then step_frame 40 (still paused) → title.